Day 24: A Heart of Compassion | Friday of the Third Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
Compassion is not weakness —
it is the heartbeat of Christ.

Welcome to Day 24 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection draws you into the very center of Jesus’ heart: a compassion that sees, feels, and moves toward others with tenderness and dignity. Not pity. Not distance. But love that notices the unseen and lifts the forgotten.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you to look at others the way Christ looks at you — with gentleness, with dignity, with a love that transforms both the giver and the receiver.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why compassion is strength, not softness

How Jesus invites you to see beneath the surface of others

Why small, hidden acts of compassion are holy

A prayer for a compassionate heart

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, make my heart compassionate.”

